{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1564881-drinkers-of-the-well","id":1564881,"title":"Drinkers of the Well","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-10-21T00:44:38-07:00","id":1564881,"title":"Drinkers of the Well","content":"One of my players has chosen the Drinkers of the Well as their tribe for my game. <br /> However I realized the Tribal Oath was never written, and having a hard time coming up with one. They'd be a Forsaken Tribe in my game, and I compared Pure and Forsaken Oaths, with it seeming that Forsaken ones tend to er more on the side of Respect; whilest Pure oaths tend towards Challenges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-21T09:25:09-07:00","id":1564896,"title":"","content":"I'm partial to &quot;Never abandon what you broke&quot;. With Drinkers' focus on constructing a new future, they run the risk of causing collateral damage when destroying the past. This Oath would prompt them to anticipate consequences of their actions, and take responsibility for them. For example, after taking out the leadership of a Cult, they can't just leave that organisation to its fate. They have to attempt to seize control of it and run it themselves, or carefully dismantle it and get the cult-members new jobs or prison sentences, or reform it in sync with the Pack's mission, or kill everyone and sell their organs on black market. You know... constructive stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-21T15:14:09-07:00","id":1564901,"title":"","content":"Oh nice. I love Acro's writeup of them. <br /> <br /> I agree with Teatime; that seems like a good oath that could have multiple interpretations the tribe could find. I like that it doesn't say improve, you could absolutely break something and ensure it stays broken, either in a bad way or a &quot;make sure it stays dead.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-21T16:50:04-07:00","id":1564902,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah that's beautiful I love it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}